        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4e1d9d67-8f98-53b8-a5e2-e993d018829f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Volkswagen CrossBlue, Honda Pilot, Volkswagen Cross Coupé GTE Concept, Volkswagen CrossBlue Coupé\n- Companies: Volkswagen, Honda, Toyota, Ford\n- Systems: VW MQB platform\n- Places: American market, Canadian market, US market, Detroit, Los Angeles\n- Events: 2015 North American International Auto Show\n\nFacts:\n- Honda introduced the Honda Pilot, a mid-size crossover SUV manufactured by Honda, in 2002.\n- Volkswagen presented the Volkswagen CrossBlue in Detroit in January 2013.\n- In the American and Canadian markets, Volkswagen CrossBlue targeted the Toyota Highlander, Toyota 4Runner, Ford Explorer, and Honda Pilot as competitors.\n- Volkswagen showed the 7-seat Volkswagen CrossBlue Coupé in Los Angeles in November 2013.\n- Volkswagen showed the Volkswagen Cross Coupé GTE Concept at the 2015 North American International Auto Show.\n- Volkswagen stated that the CrossBlue, CrossBlue Coupé, and Cross Coupé GTE together demonstrate the versatility of the VW MQB platform and are aimed at the US market.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ea50ff4a-81e6-5c3b-9517-cadb465d9170",
        "text": "Page: Volkswagen CrossBlue. Sentence: In the American and Canadian markets, its targeted competitors are the Toyota Highlander, Toyota 4Runner, Ford Explorer, and Honda Pilot.\nPage: Honda Pilot. Sentence: The Honda Pilot is a mid-size crossover SUV manufactured by Honda and introduced in 2002.\nPage: Volkswagen Cross Coupe GTE Concept. Sentence: Together, all three concept cars – the CrossBlue presented in Detroit in January 2013, the 7-seat CrossBlue Coupé shown in Los Angeles in November 2013, and the Cross Coupé GTE shown at the 2015 North American International Auto Show, it represents the versatility of using VW's MQB platform and is aimed at the US market.",
